Package: birtRcpp
Type: Package
Title: BIvariate Response Time Modeling with 'Rcpp'
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Jie-Wen", "Tsai", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "tsai.jiewen@gmail.com")
Description: Item response and response time models fitted from their full conditionals.
    Models are declared with block_model(). The main estimator is ECM (ecm(); Meng and Rubin,
    1993, <doi:10.1093/biomet/80.2.267>): one conditional maximization per block of parameters,
    Polya-Gamma bounds for logistic likelihoods (Polson, Scott and Windle, 2013,
    <doi:10.1080/01621459.2013.829001>), adaptive or Bock-Aitkin quadrature (Bock and Aitkin,
    1981, <doi:10.1007/BF02293801>) with normal-linear latent variables integrated exactly, and
    Louis' standard errors. The same steps drive Gibbs sampling (gibbs(); conjugate updates and
    Metropolis-adjusted Langevin steps) and coordinate-ascent variational inference (vi());
    mml() maximizes the same objective directly by Newton steps. Each engine has a check
    (Geweke, 2004, <doi:10.1198/016214504000001132>, and simulation-based calibration for the
    samplers) and algorithm() writes out every step. Built-in models: the two-parameter logistic
    model with log-normal response times (van der Linden, 2007, <doi:10.1007/s11336-006-1478-z>),
    latent regressions of ability and speed, cross-relations between ability and the log
    response times, and their quantile (asymmetric Laplace) versions, with samplers in C++
    ('RcppArmadillo') that port the 'Julia' package 'ExtendedRtIrtModeling.jl' (its function
    names are kept as aliases).
